33:In the current study, we aimed to elucidate the heterogeneity of MCI and identify robust subtypes of AD and MCI based on dynamic functional characteristics. A conventional timesliding windows approach was applied to construct dFC patterns and create features (23). Subsequently, we mapped individuals ' features from heterogeneous cohorts to a normative model and generated interpretable deviation features to identify potential subtypes of MCI and AD using a clustering method. The neurophysiological traits of different subtypes were analyzed based on brain morphology and cognitive scores (Figure 1).
